Yazi terminal file manager shortcuts.

Navigation
	j / k or down / up - Move through files
	h or left - Parent directory
	l or right - Enter directory
	enter - Enter directory or open the hovered file
	g p - Go to ~/Pictures
	g d - Go to ~/Downloads
	z - Find a file below the current directory with fzf
	Z - Jump using the current ~/.z Zsh-z history
	/ - Find by name in the current directory
	f - Filter the current file list
	tab - Show detailed information for the hovered file

Opening and previews
	enter on an image - View it inside Kitty with icat
	enter on a video - Play it inside Kitty with mpv
	O - Interactive Open with menu
	J / K - Seek down/up in the preview

File operations
	space - Select/unselect the hovered file
	v - Enter visual selection mode
	y - Copy selected files
	x - Cut selected files
	p - Paste copied/cut files
	r - Rename
	a - Create a file or directory (trailing / creates a directory)
	d - Move selected files to trash
	D - Permanently delete selected files
	. - Toggle hidden files

Shell and exit
	; - Run a shell command
	: - Run a shell command and block
	q - Quit and cd the shell to Yazi's current directory
	Q - Quit without changing the shell directory
	ctrl+g or command `y` - Launch Yazi
	F1 or ~ - Show Yazi help
	yazi --debug - Show terminal/image adapter diagnostics
